# --- help ---
mobbattle.help.main.1 = Dackoro's Mob Battle help
mobbattle.help.main.2 = /mobbattle give - get all thirteen wands (admin)
mobbattle.help.main.3 = /mobbattle settings - show the current settings
mobbattle.help.main.4 = /mobbattle help <topic> - more about one topic:
mobbattle.help.main.5 = wands - what each wand does
mobbattle.help.main.6 = titles - countdown, titles, cameras, music (global or per battle kind)
mobbattle.help.main.7 = chaos - Chaos Wand area and mob count
mobbattle.help.main.8 = battles - duels, rules, arenas, timers, snap, debug, stop, army
mobbattle.help.main.9 = teams - Team Wand, teams and team look
mobbattle.help.main.10 = summon - Summon Wand list
mobbattle.help.main.11 = morph - Morph, Effect, Kill wands and wand effects
mobbattle.help.main.12 = presets - default, fight, effects, debug, cinematic, your own
mobbattle.help.main.13 = config - the settings panel (every setting, lists, presets, tools)
mobbattle.help.main.14 = server - permissions, server configuration file and reload
mobbattle.help.wands.1 = Wands (/mobbattle give)
mobbattle.help.wands.2 = Battle Wand: click a mob, then another: they fight
mobbattle.help.wands.3 = crouch + click a mob: that mob vs you; click players too (playerFights duel on)
mobbattle.help.wands.4 = Army Wand: left click a mob: it joins your army (click again: leaves); right click: disband
mobbattle.help.wands.5 = your army follows you, defends you and attacks what you hit (also players)
mobbattle.help.wands.6 = Chaos Wand: left click a mob (or player): everyone attacks it
mobbattle.help.wands.7 = right click: battle royale, last one standing wins
mobbattle.help.wands.8 = Team Wand: left click adds a mob (or player) to the current team
mobbattle.help.wands.9 = right click air: next team; right click a mob: start
mobbattle.help.wands.10 = Summon Wand: left click a mob adds its type to the list
mobbattle.help.wands.11 = right click: summon the whole list
mobbattle.help.wands.12 = Morph Wand: right click copies a model, left click applies it
mobbattle.help.wands.13 = Heal / Kill / Effect / Cleanse: left click any entity
mobbattle.help.wands.14 = Effect Wand right click: next effect; Kill Wand: soul rip, then death (loot with killLoot on)
mobbattle.help.wands.15 = Snap Wand: half of the mobs turn to dust (clicked mob's battle, or every mob within snapRadius, fighting or not)
mobbattle.help.wands.16 = Debug Wand (admin): left click a mob: full report (chat, server log, debug/ file), then its target, AI state, health and effects for debugTrack seconds in the same file; right click: stop following
mobbattle.help.titles.1 = Titles and cameras (global, or per kind: <option> <duel|allVsOne|royale|teams|all> <value>; <kind> default = follow global)
mobbattle.help.titles.2 = countdown <seconds> - 3, 2, 1 before a fight starts (0 = instant)
mobbattle.help.titles.3 = startTitle on|off - title when a fight starts
mobbattle.help.titles.4 = winTitle on|off - title with the winner
mobbattle.help.titles.5 = titleStyle default|major|goblinBreach|voidEviction|random
mobbattle.help.titles.6 = titleScope owner|nearby|world - who sees fight titles
mobbattle.help.titles.7 = cameraScope owner|nearby|world - who sees the cameras (a fighter never gets the intro)
mobbattle.help.titles.8 = camera on|off - intro camera during the countdown (or cameraTime)
mobbattle.help.titles.9 = cameraStyle auto|orbit|duel|showcase|teams|focus|drone - auto: duel western, allVsOne focus, teams sweep, royale orbit
mobbattle.help.titles.10 = cameraTime <seconds> - intro camera length; 0 = the countdown; >0 films even with countdown 0
mobbattle.help.titles.11 = cameraShots <n> - showcase: how many fighters it shows (1 to maxMobs; each shot needs 1.2 s of cameraTime)
mobbattle.help.titles.12 = endCamera off|winner|lastHit - films the winner or who landed the final kill, with its kill count
mobbattle.help.titles.13 = endCameraTime <seconds> - end camera length
mobbattle.help.titles.14 = crouch while a camera plays, or skipCamera, to end it; an intro also ends when its battle ends
mobbattle.help.titles.15 = skipCamera - end your intro or end camera now
mobbattle.help.titles.16 = autoWatch on|off - start watching by yourself when the battle starts (after the countdown), for the cameraScope players; it ends the intro (default off)
mobbattle.help.titles.17 = music on|off|<track> - battle music from the countdown to the end
mobbattle.help.titles.18 = runes on|off - summoning runes and fighter marks at the start
mobbattle.help.titles.19 = e.g. countdown royale 5, cameraStyle royale showcase, camera duel off, endCamera all winner
mobbattle.help.chaos.1 = Chaos area
mobbattle.help.chaos.2 = areaStyle border|disc|discBorder|wall|off - what areas and arenas draw: border (only the border glow, default), disc (a disc on the ground), discBorder (both), wall (disc + see-through wall) or off
mobbattle.help.chaos.3 = areaColor <color>|random - palette color
mobbattle.help.chaos.4 = battleWaveTravel on|off - Snap, royale and all vs one waves: each mob is reached when the ring gets there (default off)
mobbattle.help.chaos.5 = battleWaveGroundOnly on|off - Snap, royale and all vs one waves only take mobs near the ground (default off)
mobbattle.help.chaos.6 = areaRadius <blocks> - area size
mobbattle.help.chaos.7 = areaHeight <blocks> - zone wall height (3-512)
mobbattle.help.chaos.8 = areaOnlyWand on|off - only you, only while holding the wand
mobbattle.help.chaos.9 = maxMobs <n> - mobs per click and per summon (default 200, 2-{max}; more than {warn} can lag the server)
mobbattle.help.battles.1 = Battles
mobbattle.help.battles.2 = debug - combat snapshots of 4 nearest NPCs within 20 blocks; hit log for 10s
mobbattle.help.battles.3 = debugLog on|off - battle decisions (config, arena, target choices, health scores, winner) in the server log
mobbattle.help.battles.4 = debugRecord on|off - (admin) keep the last 5 min of log and [debug] lines in memory, saved setting (default off)
mobbattle.help.battles.5 = debugDump - (admin) write what the recorder kept to debug/record_<time>.txt
mobbattle.help.battles.6 = duelMode exclusive|accumulate - replace a duel or keep connected fights
mobbattle.help.battles.7 = buff lone|streak|champion size|health|damage|defense|speed|all|off <percent> - battle buffs: lone = everyone-vs-one target, streak = per kill (up to buff streak maxKills, default 5), champion = the winners until they die or get cleansed (default 0 = none)
mobbattle.help.battles.8 = buff wand size|health|damage|defense|speed|all|off <percent> - Buff Wand, per click (default size 10, health 20, damage 10, defense 5; stacks up to buff wand maxStacks, default 5)
mobbattle.help.battles.9 = buff lone|streak|champion|wand heal on|off - that buff also fills the health (lone: heals the target when picked, even with no lone buff); default off: health keeps the same share of the new max
mobbattle.help.battles.10 = buff crown gold|<color>|off - crown on streak, champion and Buff Wand mobs (default off: the crown is the everyone-vs-one target's)
mobbattle.help.battles.11 = buff unit percent|multiplier - how buff values are shown and typed: percent (default, +100% = double) or multiplier (x2 = double, decimals like x1.5; defense x2 = half the damage taken). x2 or 50% always work
mobbattle.help.battles.12 = buff sizeMax <50-9900> - most extra size on one mob or player, all buffs together (default 200 = x3; more works but is not recommended: big players don't fit under roofs, their camera ends up in blocks). Jumps grow with the size
mobbattle.help.battles.13 = buff sizeSpeed off|natural|strong|full - how much a size buff speeds up: natural = x4 twice as fast (default), strong = x4 2.8x, full = x4 4x (steps match the ground)
mobbattle.help.battles.14 = buff sizeJump off|natural|strong|full - how much a size buff raises the jump: natural = the height grows with the size (default)
mobbattle.help.battles.15 = fightLaser on|off - laser between fighters at the start (per kind too)
mobbattle.help.battles.16 = fightLaserColor <color>|random - laser color (palette; random = a bright one each fight)
mobbattle.help.battles.17 = battleIsolation <duel|allVsOne|royale|teams|all> on|off - outside mobs cannot hurt battle mobs
mobbattle.help.battles.18 = selfDefense <duel|allVsOne|royale|teams|all> on|off - a mob hit by an enemy that isn't its target turns on it (default on)
mobbattle.help.battles.19 = friendlyFire <allVsOne|teams|all> on|off - allies hurt each other
mobbattle.help.battles.20 = playerFights <duel|allVsOne|royale|teams|all> on|off - players fight too (default on, never in Creative):
mobbattle.help.battles.21 = the wands work on players like on mobs; crouch + Battle Wand on a mob: it vs you
mobbattle.help.battles.22 = chaos me - every mob in the area attacks you (playerFights allVsOne on)
mobbattle.help.battles.23 = battlePvp on|off - enemy players in a battle hurt each other even with the world's PvP off
mobbattle.help.battles.24 = arena <kind|all> on|show|wall|off - area drawn the whole fight (show), nobody leaves it (wall), both (on)
mobbattle.help.battles.25 = arenaSize <blocks>|auto - arena radius of duels and team battles (Chaos Wand: areaRadius)
mobbattle.help.battles.26 = timer <kind|all> <time>|off - time limit with a timer box: 90, 2m, 1m30s, --minutes=2 --seconds=30
mobbattle.help.battles.27 = scoreboard <kind|all> on|off - HUD with one row per side: teams alive/total and kills, target health vs attackers, royale left + top killers, duel health (default teams on)
mobbattle.help.battles.28 = wave <summon|snap|slam|allVsOne|royale|all> <color|off> - ground shockwave color per action (palette colors; default summon green, snap white, slam/royale purple, allVsOne yellow)
mobbattle.help.battles.29 = mobFx <duel|allVsOne|attackers|royale|all> <color|default|off> - tint, aura and rune on the battle mobs (default = original look; royale purple by default)
mobbattle.help.battles.30 = crown gold|<color>|off - everyone vs one: crown with rays of light over the lone target for 20 s (default gold)
mobbattle.help.battles.31 = cleanseColor <color> - Cleanse Wand look: light from above, burst, aura and rune (default white)
mobbattle.help.battles.32 = cleanseArea on|off - Cleanse Wand: hold left click to cleanse every mob and player around you (default on)
mobbattle.help.battles.33 = cleanseRadius <blocks> - reach of the held-click cleanse (default 12)
mobbattle.help.battles.34 = cleanseAreaSelf on|off - the held-click cleanse cleanses you too (default off)
mobbattle.help.battles.35 = healLight <color>|off - Heal Wand: a light comes down from the sky and the heal lands with it (default green; off = at once)
mobbattle.help.battles.36 = buffLook shimmer|runes|off - look of a buffed mob while the buff lasts: shimmer (veins, eye flames, runes; default), runes (only eye flames and runes) or off
mobbattle.help.battles.37 = buffLight buff|<color>|off - Buff Wand: a light comes down from the sky and the buff lands with it (default buff = in buffColor; off = at once)
mobbattle.help.battles.38 = buffColor <color> - buff look: the Buff Wand's mark and swirl, and the shimmer (veins, eye flames, runes) of buffed mobs (default purple; taking the buff off is grey)
mobbattle.help.battles.39 = borderColor <summon|snap|slam|allVsOne|royale|all> <color|off|area> - border glow color per action (area = areaColor; default summon green, allVsOne yellow, royale purple, snap/slam off: a color draws a ring at their reach)
mobbattle.help.battles.40 = arenaShrink <kind|all> on|off - the arena closes in like a battle royale zone (default: royale on)
mobbattle.help.battles.41 = arenaShrinkTo <blocks> - final radius of a closing arena (default 15)
mobbattle.help.battles.42 = arenaShrinkTime <90|2m|1m30s> - how long a closing arena takes when the battle has no timer (default 2m)
mobbattle.help.battles.43 = unstick on|off - a mob stuck 10 s on another level (cave, mountain; fliers 20 s, walls too) appears next to its opponent
mobbattle.help.battles.44 = standoffTime <seconds>|off - a mob on its opponent's level that this long gets no closer, hits nothing and isn't hit gets shoved toward it (0-3600, default 15, 0 = off)
mobbattle.help.battles.45 = passiveWinIgnore <role,role*,...>|none - roles that never let passiveWin end a battle while one is alive, e.g. training dummies (default Test_Dummy*; * = any ending)
mobbattle.help.battles.46 = idleEnd <seconds>|off - a battle where no fighter hurts an enemy for this long ends in a draw (0-3600, default 150 = 2.5 min, 0 = off)
mobbattle.help.battles.47 = passiveWin <seconds>|off - when only one side can still fight back (the rest are passive mobs), it wins after this long without a hit; nobody can fight = draw; an alert shows bottom left (0-3600, default 15, 0 = off)
mobbattle.help.battles.48 = duelCard on|off - read-only card with both fighters' stats (health, attack, defense, size, with their buffs) in a 1 vs 1 duel, from the countdown to the end (default off)
mobbattle.help.battles.49 = focusCard on|off - read-only card in an all vs one: the lone target's stats (health, attack, defense, size, kills) and the attackers left, their health and the top damage dealer (default off)
mobbattle.help.battles.50 = judgeBy <kind|all> health|damage|kills|mix - what timeUp health/judge scores: health % left (default), share of the damage or kills (per fighter, so bigger sides don't win for size), or the three averaged
mobbattle.help.battles.51 = tieBreak [kind] damage|kills|random|draw - who wins when the judgeBy score is even at time up (the same as judgeBy, damage or kills, takes the other one; default damage, per battle kind too)
mobbattle.help.battles.52 = killTieBreak [kind] damage|alive|first|shared - kill table order for fighters with the same kills: more damage dealt (default), standing fighters first, who got there first, or a shared place (per battle kind too)
mobbattle.help.battles.53 = snap - half of the mobs within snapRadius (fighting or not) turn to dust, like the Snap Wand
mobbattle.help.battles.54 = snapMode global|team - half of everyone, or half of each side
mobbattle.help.battles.55 = snapPercent <1-100> - share that turns to dust (default 50)
mobbattle.help.battles.56 = snapTime <1-600> - seconds over which they turn to dust (default 5)
mobbattle.help.battles.57 = snapHitDelay <ms> - Snap Wand: wait after the click until the slam hits and the snap fires (default 310, 0-2000)
mobbattle.help.battles.58 = snapRadius <blocks> - snap reach without battles (default 60, separate from areaRadius)
mobbattle.help.battles.59 = snapPlayers on|off - the snap takes players in reach too (never you, never Creative; default on)
mobbattle.help.battles.60 = timerStyle custom|portal - our own timer box (default) or the game's Void portal box
mobbattle.help.battles.61 = timeUp <kind|all> draw|kill|continue|health|judge - when the timer ends (health: the best judgeBy score wins, default most health in %; judge: and the losers die, the winners heal)
mobbattle.help.battles.62 = watch - spectate the nearest running battle (yours first), even after it started: the camera follows a fighter
mobbattle.help.battles.63 = right click: nearest fighter (not seen yet), left click: back to the previous one, mouse: turn the camera, Q or watch exit: leave
mobbattle.help.battles.64 = when the fighter dies the camera goes to its killer; a card shows its stats; after the battle you come back
mobbattle.help.battles.65 = stop - end every battle, countdown, timer box, arena, camera shot, battle music and watch
mobbattle.help.battles.66 = skipTimer - every running timer jumps to 0: the battles end by their timeUp rule (draw, judge...)
mobbattle.help.battles.67 = army clearAll - disband every player's army
mobbattle.help.battles.68 = armyTint on|off - army mobs wear a tint while in your army (default off)
mobbattle.help.battles.69 = armyTintColor <color> - the army tint color, a palette color (default blue)
mobbattle.help.battles.71 = armyFriendlyFire on|off - hits inside one army (mates, a leader and its mobs) do damage, but they stay allies (default off)
mobbattle.help.battles.72 = battleBelow <blocks>|off / battleAbove <blocks>|off - how far below / above its center a royale or all vs one takes mobs (default 50 / 40)
mobbattle.help.battles.73 = arenaVertical <blocks>|off - how far above or below the arena's level a fighter may go before the wall brings it back; fliers never (default off)
mobbattle.help.battles.70 = resetAll - stop + teams clearAll + army clearAll + morph reset
mobbattle.help.teams.1 = Teams
mobbattle.help.teams.2 = teams list - show the teams
mobbattle.help.teams.3 = teams auto - put mobs in range into teams: summon team rules first, the rest one team per type (one type: split in two)
mobbattle.help.teams.4 = teams start - start the team battle
mobbattle.help.teams.5 = teams clear - empty your teams
mobbattle.help.teams.6 = teams clearAll - empty every player's teams
mobbattle.help.teams.7 = teams join <team> / leave - fight with a team yourself (playerFights teams on)
mobbattle.help.teams.8 = teams add <name> <color> - new team
mobbattle.help.teams.9 = teams color <team> <color> / rename <team> <name>
mobbattle.help.teams.10 = teams remove <team> / reset - back to the 4 defaults
mobbattle.help.teams.11 = teamLook both|tint|mist|off - how team mobs look
mobbattle.help.teams.12 = teamLook time <seconds>|infinite - how long it stays
mobbattle.help.teams.13 = teamLook onlyWand on|off - only while holding the Team Wand
mobbattle.help.teams.14 = teamByType on|off - clicking a mob brings every mob of its type within areaRadius into the team
mobbattle.help.summon.1 = Summon list
mobbattle.help.summon.2 = summon - summon the list around you
mobbattle.help.summon.3 = summon list - show the list
mobbattle.help.summon.4 = summon add <role> [count|random] [team] - the same mob and team adds to that entry's count; another team is one more entry (Skeleton_Archer#2)
mobbattle.help.summon.5 = summon modify <entry|role> [team|none] <count|random> - sets an exact count
mobbattle.help.summon.6 = summon remove <entry> / clear
mobbattle.help.summon.7 = summon team <entry> <team|none> - team rule
mobbattle.help.summon.8 = summon random <min> <max> - range for random counts
mobbattle.help.summon.9 = summonRadius <blocks>|auto - summon area size (auto grows with the count)
mobbattle.help.summon.10 = summon atLeastOne true|false - random types spawn 1+
mobbattle.help.summon.11 = summonDespawn never|battleEnd|timer - summons leave on their own: never (default, they stay), battleEnd (the surviving summons of a battle go when it ends), timer (each goes summonLifetime seconds after it spawned)
mobbattle.help.summon.12 = summonLifetime <seconds> - how long a summon lives with summonDespawn timer (5-3600, default 60)
mobbattle.help.summon.13 = summonExit disintegrate|vanish|shatter - how summons leave: disintegrate like the Kill Wand (soul rip, no loot, default), vanish at once (no loot) or shatter like jade glass (no loot)
mobbattle.help.summon.14 = summonCalm off|summons|all - summons wait calm until a battle, wand fight or army takes them: summons = they ignore each other, all = players and other mobs too; a hit lets one fight back its attacker (default off)
mobbattle.help.summon.15 = summonArmy on|off - summoned mobs join your army, like the Army Wand (default off)
mobbattle.help.summon.16 = summonJade on|off - summons come out wearing the jade look, like the Effect Wand's (default off)
mobbattle.help.summon.17 = summonJadeColor <color> - the summons' jade color, a palette color (default green)
mobbattle.help.summon.18 = summon fill <types> [each:<n>] [teams:<n>] [mod:..] [type:..] [group:..] [add] - random mobs that fight, of similar strength (max health), into the list; teams:2 deals them into balanced teams; replaces the list unless add
mobbattle.help.morph.1 = Morph and effects
mobbattle.help.morph.2 = morph <model> - set the Morph Wand model
mobbattle.help.morph.3 = morph list [text] - search model IDs
mobbattle.help.morph.4 = morph reset - every morphed mob gets its model back
mobbattle.help.morph.5 = wandEffect <id> - Effect Wand effect, e.g. Burn; A>B>C gives each when the previous ends; jade[:color], shimmer[:color]
mobbattle.help.morph.6 = waveTravel on|off - wand waves (Morph, Cleanse, Effect, Heal): each mob is hit when the ring reaches it, not all at once (default on)
mobbattle.help.morph.7 = waveGroundOnly on|off - wand waves only hit mobs near the ground, as the game's slams; fliers and caves are spared (default off)
mobbattle.help.morph.8 = healArea on|off - Heal Wand: hold left click to slam the ground and heal every mob and player around you, you too (default on)
mobbattle.help.morph.9 = healRadius <blocks> - reach of the held-click heal (default 12)
mobbattle.help.morph.10 = healAreaSelf on|off - the held-click heal heals you too (default on)
mobbattle.help.morph.11 = effectAreaSelf on|off - the held-click effect wave gives you the effect too (default off)
mobbattle.help.morph.12 = effectArea on|off - Effect Wand: hold left click to give the effect to every mob and player around you (default on)
mobbattle.help.morph.13 = effectRadius <blocks> - reach of the held-click effect wave (default 12)
mobbattle.help.morph.14 = wandFx on|off - glow, soul rip, charm, summoning runes... on the clicked mob
mobbattle.help.morph.15 = killDelay <seconds> - Kill Wand soul rip before death (0-3, 0 = instant)
mobbattle.help.morph.16 = killHitDelay <ms> - Kill Wand: wait after the click until the cast hits; Hakai sound and disintegration start then (default 175, 0-2000)
mobbattle.help.morph.17 = killLoot on|off - mobs killed by the Kill Wand or Snap drop their loot (default off)
mobbattle.help.morph.18 = lookGlow <0-15> - light around mobs with a jade/shimmer look or the buff's shimmer, in its color (default 6, 0 = off)
mobbattle.help.morph.19 = deathGlow <0-15> - Kill Wand: the disintegrating mob flashes in its color, fading out (default 12, 0 = off)
mobbattle.help.morph.20 = killPlayers on|off - the Kill Wand works on players too: they disintegrate, then die normally (default on)
mobbattle.help.morph.21 = morphPlayers on|off - the Morph Wand works on players too (default on)
mobbattle.help.morph.22 = morphBurst on|off - Morph Wand: hold left click to send a wave that gives every mob around your copied model (default on)
mobbattle.help.morph.23 = morphShuffle on|off - Morph Wand: hold right click to send a wave that swaps the models of the mobs around in random pairs (default on)
mobbattle.help.morph.24 = morphBurstRadius <blocks> - reach of the held-click waves (default 12)
mobbattle.help.morph.25 = morphBurstSelf on|off - the held-click morph and swap waves change you too (default off)
mobbattle.help.morph.26 = debugTrack <seconds> - Debug Wand: how long a left-clicked mob is followed after its report (0-600, default 30, 0 = report only)
mobbattle.help.morph.27 = eyeTest [<color>|off] - (experimental, admin) recolors the eyes of the nearest mob (8 blocks) with a texture made at runtime (palette color, default Purple); off puts the original models back
mobbattle.help.presets.1 = Presets
mobbattle.help.presets.2 = preset list - built-in and saved presets
mobbattle.help.presets.3 = preset default - every setting back to default (team and summon lists stay)
mobbattle.help.presets.4 = preset fight - just the fights: no countdown, cameras, titles, music, lasers, runes, waves, borders, mob looks, crown, drawings or timers
mobbattle.help.presets.5 = preset effects - countdown 3, 2 min timer (most health wins; royale keeps 3 min judge), titles, music, runes, area discBorder, waves, borders, mob looks, scoreboards; no cameras or lasers
mobbattle.help.presets.6 = preset debug - everything visible: area wall, waves, borders, mob looks, lasers, runes, arenas, team look both, duel card, scoreboards (presets never change the debug log: it's admin only)
mobbattle.help.presets.7 = preset cinematic - countdown 5, cameras (duel western, royale drone, allVsOne focus, teams sweep), end camera with kill count, music, area, waves, arenas, mob looks and crown; no lasers, runes or border glow
mobbattle.help.presets.8 = preset save <name> / load <name> / delete <name> - your own presets
mobbattle.help.presets.9 = reset effects|cameras|titles|arenas|rules|wands|all - only that group of settings back to default
mobbattle.help.server.1 = Server setup
mobbattle.help.server.2 = permissions open|server - open lets anyone use and configure; server checks use/config grants
mobbattle.help.server.3 = dackoro.mob_battle.use - wands and player-started battles (default hytale:Adventurer)
mobbattle.help.server.4 = dackoro.mob_battle.config - settings, presets and team/summon configuration (default hytale:Admin)
mobbattle.help.server.5 = dackoro.mob_battle.admin - stop, resetAll, skipTimer, army clearAll, teams clearAll, teams reset, morph reset, apply, debug log, reload, give, permissions and events (default hytale:Admin; required in both modes)
mobbattle.help.server.6 = config/panel opens the settings panel for reading in either mode; saving needs config when server mode is on.
mobbattle.help.server.7 = The panel Admin tab is separate and shown only to players with the real admin permission, even in open mode.
mobbattle.help.server.8 = permissions open|server, reload, stop, resetAll, skipTimer, army clearAll, teams clearAll, teams reset, morph reset, give, debug log, and server events remain admin-only in both modes.
mobbattle.help.server.9 = Pure settings work from the server console. Position-based actions need a player.
mobbattle.help.server.10 = Server settings are in the plugin data directory's fx.properties; edit it while the server is stopped, then run /mobbattle reload.
mobbattle.help.server.11 = reload - reload fx.properties from disk (admin)
mobbattle.help.server.12 = measure [look|id:<uuid>|last] [seconds] | measure stop - speed (blocks/s) and jump height of you, the mob you look at or an entity by id (works from the console), in chat, for 10 s by default, up to 60 (admin; to calibrate size and speed buffs)
mobbattle.help.server.13 = test spawn <role> <here|x y z> [count] [world] [calm] | test list | test clear - test mobs, with their ids (admin; last = the newest)
mobbattle.help.server.14 = test walk <id|last> <x> <z> - a test mob walks to that block (only roles with a path behaviour, mostly bosses)
mobbattle.help.server.15 = test chase <id|last> <here|x y z> - a still training dummy there, and the mob runs to attack it (any mob that can attack)
mobbattle.help.server.16 = test duel <roleA> <roleB> <distance> <here|x y z> [world] - spawns both, starts a duel and logs every hit (damage, reach) and a summary
mobbattle.help.server.17 = test perf <role> <count> <here|x y z> [world] - the world's tick time over 10 s before and after spawning them
mobbattle.help.server.18 = test royale <role:count+...> <here|x y z> <radius> [world] - spawns the mix and starts a battle royale, summary at the end
mobbattle.help.server.19 = test wave <heal|cleanse|effect|morph|shuffle> <here|x y z> [world] [effect|model] - a wand's held-click wave from that spot: how many it reached and when
mobbattle.help.server.20 = test stats <id|last> - health, size, buffs, effects, battle, calm, army and model in one line
mobbattle.help.server.21 = test verify <here|x y z> [mod:<name>|mod:hytale] [type:<fighters|defend|noattack>] [text] [time:<s>] [batch:<n>] - each role is ordered to attack a still dummy; says which Type guesses were wrong (report in tests/)
mobbattle.help.server.22 = test roles [mod:<name>|mod:hytale] [type:<fighters|defend|noattack|avoid>] [text] - the mob roles the panel's Show filters keep, with mod and type
mobbattle.help.server.23 = test expect <id|last> <field> <=|!=|>|<|>=|<=> <value> - a check (alive, health, maxhealth, healthpct, size, buff.<stat>, effect, battle, team, calm, army, morphed, model, x, y, z); scripts count them
mobbattle.help.server.24 = test camera <orbit|duel|showcase|teams|focus|drone> <player> [seconds] - that intro camera over the test mobs, for that player
mobbattle.help.server.25 = test snapshot [name] | test restore [name] - save fx.properties (settings, teams, summon list) and put it back
mobbattle.help.server.26 = test run <script> | test stop - runs <data dir>/tests/<script>.txt: one command per line, wait <seconds>, say <text>, # comments
mobbattle.help.server.27 = apply <player|me|look|near <radius>|players|id:<uuid>|last> <action> [value] - a wand action on chosen players or mobs (admin): buff <clicks>, size|health|damage|defense <value>, unbuff, heal, cleanse, effect <id>, look jade|shimmer[:color], morph <model|player>, unmorph, army add|remove, team <team|none>
mobbattle.help.server.28 = The permissions mode is saved in fx.properties and presets/reset preserve it; change it explicitly with the admin-only permissions command.
mobbattle.help.server.29 = event duel <uuidA> <uuidB> [world] - start an ownerless NPC duel
mobbattle.help.server.30 = event royale <x> <y> <z> <radius> [maxMobs] [world] - start an ownerless NPC royale
mobbattle.help.server.31 = event focus <uuid> [world] - nearby NPCs attack the specified NPC
mobbattle.help.server.32 = event list [radius] - show nearby NPC UUIDs (admin; player only)
mobbattle.help.config.1 = Configuration panel
mobbattle.help.config.2 = /mobbattle config or /mobbattle panel - open the settings panel; both commands are public for reading.
mobbattle.help.config.3 = Left menu: Presentation, Cameras, Battles, one tab per battle kind (Duel, All vs one, Royale, Team battles),
mobbattle.help.config.4 = Chaos area, Colors & looks, Buffs, Wands, Teams, Summon list, Presets & reset, Tools, Admin. Every setting the commands change is there.
mobbattle.help.config.5 = Changing a value only marks it (gold): Save changes applies them all at once, Discard changes drops them.
mobbattle.help.config.6 = Presets and Reset buttons fill the form first, so you can check them before saving.
mobbattle.help.config.7 = Team list, summon list, tools and admin buttons run their command at once (chat shows the result).
mobbattle.help.config.8 = In server mode saving needs dackoro.mob_battle.config; the Admin page needs dackoro.mob_battle.admin.
mobbattle.help.config.9 = Admin is a separate tab, visible only with a real dackoro.mob_battle.admin grant in either permissions mode.
mobbattle.help.config.10 = Admin page: permissions open|server, reload, give, end timers, royale event, stop, armies, teams, morphs, resetAll.
